From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: reset software ring pointers before recovery suspend

The A3xx recovery callback resets CP before adreno_recover() invokes the
GPU-specific suspend callback. The hardware read/write pointers are then
zero, but a3xx_idle() compares RPTR with the old software ring write
pointer.
On SM-T531 a GPU hang is followed by a 0/0x24 ring-drain timeout, causing
suspend to return -EBUSY instead of reaching the normal power-cycle path.

Synchronize the software ring cursors with the reset hardware before the
suspend/idle check. Fence state and pending submission lists are unchanged;
recover_worker() remains responsible for replay after hardware reinit.
This addresses the secondary recovery failure, not the original GPU hang.

Normal runtime/system suspend still drains the live ring and VBIF. No
clock, voltage or power-management policy is changed.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
@@ -361,6 +361,7 @@
 
 static void a3xx_recover(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
+	struct msm_ringbuffer *ring = gpu->rb[0];
 	int i;
 
 	adreno_dump_info(gpu);
@@ -377,6 +378,15 @@
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 1);
 	gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD);
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 0);
+
+	/*
+	 * Reset discards the ring and clears the hardware pointers. Match the
+	 * software write pointer before adreno_recover() calls pm_suspend(),
+	 * whose idle check would otherwise wait for the discarded commands.
+	 * recover_worker() replays the remaining submissions after reinit.
+	 */
+	ring->cur = ring->next = ring->start;
+
 	adreno_recover(gpu);
 }
 
